TASK 1 — Deploy Flask Backend + Express Frontend on Single EC2
STEP 1 — Create EC2 Instance
Open AWS Console
Go to EC2
Launch Instance

Settings:

Name: assignment-ec2
AMI: Ubuntu Server 24.04 LTS
Instance Type: t3.micro
Create/download key pair (Harsh.pem)

Security Group Inbound Rules:

SSH → 22
HTTP → 80
Custom TCP → 3000
Custom TCP → 5000
STEP 2 — Connect to EC2
ssh -i Harsh.pem ubuntu@YOUR-PUBLIC-IP
STEP 3 — Install Packages
sudo apt update
sudo apt install git python3 python3-pip python3-venv nodejs npm nginx -y
STEP 4 — Clone Repository
git clone https://github.com/helloworld5647/tutedude-devops.git
STEP 5 — Start Flask Backend
cd tutedude-devops/backend


python3 -m venv venv


source venv/bin/activate


pip install -r requirements.txt


python3 app.py

Expected:

Backend running on port 5000
STEP 6 — Start Express Frontend

Open another SSH terminal:

cd ~/tutedude-devops/frontend


npm install


npm start

Expected:

Frontend running on port 3000
STEP 7 — Access Application

Frontend:

http://YOUR-PUBLIC-IP:3000

Backend:

http://YOUR-PUBLIC-IP:5000
